 /* GPU priority of the capture and encoding work: during a game that keeps
  * the card busy, the copy, the conversion and the encoding would otherwise
- * wait behind its frames (up to one game frame). Process class HIGH through
- * D3DKMTSetProcessSchedulingPriorityClass (gdi32.dll, loaded at run time),
- * never REALTIME: Microsoft warns that it can make the system unusable, and
- * it is the suspect of two TDR freezes (0x116, nvlddmkm) right after a
- * Station update on an NVIDIA card. Then IDXGIDevice::SetGPUThreadPriority(7)
- * on `device`, as Sunshine does with HIGH. The hardware-accelerated GPU
- * scheduling mode is only read, for the log. `buf` gets the log line. */
-enum { KN_KMT_PRIORITY_HIGH = 4 };
+ * wait behind its frames (up to one game frame). `level` comes from
+ * [kyavserver] gpu_priority (KyberNow 0024):
+ *  - KN_GPU_PRIORITY_NORMAL: nothing changed, Windows' own scheduling (as
+ *    in Kyber);
+ *  - KN_GPU_PRIORITY_HIGH, the default: process class HIGH through
+ *    D3DKMTSetProcessSchedulingPriorityClass (gdi32.dll, loaded at run time);
+ *  - KN_GPU_PRIORITY_REALTIME: process class REALTIME, HIGH if Windows
+ *    refuses it. The work then always goes before a game's frames, but
+ *    Microsoft warns that it can make the system unusable, and it is the
+ *    suspect of two TDR freezes (0x116, nvlddmkm) right after a Station
+ *    update on an NVIDIA card: only when asked.
+ * Then, unless NORMAL, IDXGIDevice::SetGPUThreadPriority(7) on `device`, as
+ * Sunshine does. The hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling mode is only read,
+ * for the log. `buf` gets the log line. */
+enum { KN_GPU_PRIORITY_NORMAL, KN_GPU_PRIORITY_HIGH, KN_GPU_PRIORITY_REALTIME };
+enum { KN_KMT_PRIORITY_HIGH = 4, KN_KMT_PRIORITY_REALTIME = 5 };
